    "b-res",
    "b-l",
    "b-paid"
   ],
   "so": {
    "figures": {},
    "literals": [],
    "text": "A reserve asks taxpayers once, and afterwards only for what was actually used."
   },
   "text": "Held once as a reserve, the same protection raises $1,458,783: $223,774 up front, then refills."
  },
  {
   "figures": {},
   "literals": [],
   "notes": [
    {
     "figures": {},
     "kind": "measured",
     "literals": [],
     "text": "Money in a budget line is moved between lines by School Committee transfer during the year."
    },
    {
     "cite": {
      "href": "/docs/meetings/text/select-board/2025-10-07-minutes-7441.txt",
      "label": "Select Board minutes, 2025-10-07"
     },
     "figures": {},
     "kind": "quote",
     "literals": [],
     "text": "The fund requires a majority vote of both boards to expend."
    }
   ],
   "rests_on": [
    "b-l"
   ],
   "so": {
    "figures": {},
    "literals": [],
    "text": "A reserve is set aside for this and nothing else; a budget line can be spent on whatever else runs short first."
   },
   "text": "A reserve is spent only by a majority of both the School Committee and the Select Board."
  },
  {
   "figures": {
    "a": {
     "text": "11",
     "unit": "",
     "value": 11
    },
    "n": {
     "text": "17",
